// Was SOUNDNESS QUEUE row fn_item_pointer_call_where_static_admits; closed 2026-09-23: a call through a fn-item value is judged by the named function's declaration, its where-clause included.
// SOUNDNESS QUEUE row fn_item_pointer_call_where_static_admits (tier 2).
// NEIGHBOUR of bc_admits regions-static-bound, ROWED — reason 1 (the fact has no
// carrier there). A fn item bound to a local and called through it goes through the
// closure / fn-pointer invoke, whose type carries parameter types and a return but
// NO where-clause, so the callee's `'a: 'static` cannot be asked at that call.
// Rust keeps the fn-item type (and its bounds) and refuses: E0521.
package fn_item_pointer_call_where_static_fail;
fn static_id<'a>(t: &'a i64) -> i64 where 'a: 'static { return *t; }
fn f(u: &i64) -> i64 {
    let g = static_id;
    return g(u);
}
fn main() -> i32 { let n = 1i64; return f(&n) as i32; }
// rustc 1.98.1 --edition 2024 (round 2026-09-15f-rustcaudit, class CONFIRMED): REFUSED — error: lifetime may not live long enough. Twin src/compiler/probes/2026-09-15f-rustcaudit/rust/fn_item_pointer_call_where_static_admits.rs. Audit note: header says E0521; rustc 1.98.1 prints an uncoded lifetime error.
